<header><h1>Council Keleres</h1></header>
<article>
<h2 id="the-tribunii"><a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Council_Keleres#Codex_III:~:text=The%20Tribunii">The Tribunii</a></h2>
    <ol class="note">
    <li>The Keleres player chooses their starting technology after all other players have gained their starting technologies.<sup>2,4</sup></li>
    <li>If there is only one unique starting technology among those owned by other players, the Keleres player will start the game with only one technology.<sup>4</sup></li>
    </ol>

<h2 id="council-patronage"><a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Council_Keleres#Codex_III:~:text=Council%20Patronage">Council Patronage</a></h2>
    <ol class="note">
    <li>The Keleres player must mandatorily replenish their commodities and gain a trade good every strategy phase.<sup>12</sup></li>
    <li>If the Keleres player already has their maximum number of commodities, they will still replenish their commodities during the strategy phase. This will not give them additional commodities, but will trigger any effects that happen when the Keleres player replenishes their commodities.<sup>1</sup></li>
    </ol>

<h2 id="laws-order"><a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Council_Keleres#Codex_III:~:text=Law%27s%20Order">Law&rsquo;s Order</a></h2>
    <ol class="note">
    <li>If this ability is used, all laws are blanked. The Keleres player cannot choose for some laws to remain in effect.<sup>4,12</sup></li>
    <li>The Keleres player and all of the other players treat all laws as blank for the turn.<sup>4</sup></li>
    <li>The blanked laws come back into effect at the end of the turn.<sup>4,12</sup></li>
    <li>If the Keleres player owns the <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Agenda_Cards#New_Agendas:~:text=Political%20Censure"><i>Political Censure</i></a> law, they will not lose a victory point when it is blanked, and they may use action cards during this turn.<sup>*</sup></li>
    <ol><li>If the Keleres player then uses the <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Action_Cards#Twilight_Imperium_Fourth_Edition:~:text=Repeal%20Law"><i>Repeal Law</i></a> action card, targeting the <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Agenda_Cards#New_Agendas:~:text=Political%20Censure"><i>Political Censure</i></a> law, then it will be discarded without the Keleres player losing the victory point.<sup>*</sup></li></ol>
    </ol>

<h2 id="keleres-rider"><a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Council_Keleres#Faction_Promissory_Note:~:text=Keleres%20Rider">Keleres Rider</a> <sub>(Promissory Note)</sub></h2>
    <ol class="note">
    <li>After playing <i>Keleres Rider</i>, a player may use additional abilities, including playing other rider cards.<sup>2</sup></li>
    <ol><li>Any other riders may be played to predict the same or a different outcome.<sup>1,2</sup></li></ol>
    <li>The effect of a successful <i>Keleres Rider</i> will be resolved after the effect of the agenda.<sup>2</sup></li>
    <li>A player who cannot vote may still play a <i>Keleres Rider</i>.<sup>1</sup></li>
    <li>A player who cannot play action cards may still play a <i>Keleres Rider</i>.<sup>*</sup></li>
    </ol>

<h2 id="agency-supply-network"><a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Council_Keleres#Thunder's_Edge_2:~:text=Agency%20Supply%20Network">Agency Supply Network</a> <sub>(Technology)</sub></h2>
    <ol class="note">
    <li>Any abilities that trigger &ldquo;when/after a unit uses <a href="/R_production"><sc>Production</sc></a>&rdquo; will trigger an additional time, for example, the <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Cybernetic_Technologies#Sarween_Tools"><i>Sarween Tools</i></a> technology.<sup>4</sup></li>
    <li>The additional <a href="/R_production"><sc>Production</sc></a> ability cannot belong to the same unit as the original <a href="/R_production"><sc>Production</sc></a> ability.<sup>4</sup></li>
    <ol><li>During a tactical action, the active player must use every <a href="/R_production"><sc>Production</sc></a> ability of their units in the active system, or none of them. As such, the additional <a href="/R_production"><sc>Production</sc></a> ability must belong to a unit in a different system.<sup>4</sup></li></ol>
    <li>The Keleres player may use <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Council_Keleres#Faction_Specific_Components:~:text=Custodia%20Vigilia">Custodia Vigilia</a> as the additional <a href="/R_production"><sc>Production</sc></a> ability, and when they use <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Council_Keleres#Faction_Specific_Components:~:text=Custodia%20Vigilia">Custodia Vigilia</a> as the original <a href="/R_production"><sc>Production</sc></a> ability, they may use an additional <a href="/R_production"><sc>Production</sc></a> ability.<sup>*</sup></li>
    <li>The original <a href="/R_production"><sc>Production</sc></a> ability must be fully resolved, before the Keleres player may use an additional <a href="/R_production"><sc>Production</sc></a> ability.<sup>*</sup></li>
    <ol><li>The Keleres player cannot pay one resource for two fighters or infantry, then place one with a unit using the original <a href="/R_production"><sc>Production</sc></a> ability and one with the unit using the additional <a href="/R_production"><sc>Production</sc></a> ability.<sup>*</sup></li></ol>
    </ol>

<h2 id="executive-order"><a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Council_Keleres#Thunder's_Edge_2:~:text=Executive%20Order">Executive Order</a> <sub>(Technology)</sub></h2>
    <ol class="note">
    <li>Riders may be played when resolving <i>Executive Order</i>.<sup>2,6,9</sup></li>
    <li>If the Keleres player draws one of the <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Agenda_Cards#Directives:~:text=Classified%20Document%20Leaks"><i>Classified Document Leaks</i></a>, <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Agenda_Cards#Directives:~:text=Judicial%20Abolishment"><i>Judicial Abolishment</i></a>, <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Agenda_Cards#Directives:~:text=Miscount%20Disclosed"><i>Miscount Disclosed</i></a> or <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Agenda_Cards#Directives:~:text=New%20Constitution"><i>New Constitution</i></a> agendas, they will discard it if required and reveal a new agenda from the deck.<sup>*</sup></li>
    <li>If the <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Agenda_Cards#Directives:~:text=Miscount%20Disclosed"><i>Miscount Disclosed</i></a> agenda is resolved, the players will also vote on the elected agenda during the Keleres player&rsquo;s action.<sup>*</sup></li>
    <li>If an agenda would give multiple players a victory point, those players gain that victory point in initiative order, starting with the player with the <a href="/R_leadership"><i>Leadership</i></a> strategy card (or next lowest initiative value should no player have the <a href="/R_leadership"><i>Leadership</i></a> strategy card), regardless of the Keleres player&rsquo;s initiative.<sup>*</sup></li>
    <li>Players exhaust planets to cast votes when resolving <i>Executive Order</i>, even if the <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Agenda_Cards#Directives:~:text=Representative%20Government"><i>Representative Government</i></a> law is in play, which only affects voting during the agenda phase.<sup>6</sup></li>
    <li>If a third law is put into play, the <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Objectives#Agenda_Phase:~:text=Dictate%20Policy"><i>Dictate Policy</i></a> secret objective cannot be scored until the agenda phase.<sup>2</sup></li>
    <li>The <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Objectives#Agenda_Phase:~:text=Drive%20the%20Debate"><i>Drive the Debate</i></a> secret objective cannot be scored while resolving <i>Executive Order</i>.<sup>2</sup></li>
    <li>Effects from agenda outcomes that occur &ldquo;at the end of this agenda phase&rdquo; will instead resolve at the end of the next agenda phase.<sup>6,7</sup></li>
    <li>Effects from agenda outcomes that occur &ldquo;at the start of the next strategy phase&rdquo; will still resolve at the start of the next strategy phase.<sup>6</sup></li>
    <li>When resolving <i>Executive Order</i>, the <a href="/F_argent">Argent</a> player does not vote first, but still casts additional votes.<sup>2,6</sup></li>
    </ol>

<h2 id="i-i-h-q-modernization"><a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Council_Keleres#Codex_III_2:~:text=I.I.H.Q.%20Modernization">I.I.H.Q. Modernization</a> <sub>(Technology/Breakthrough)</sub></h2>
    <ol class="note">
    <li>If the Keleres player is neighbors with another player, that player is neighbors with the Keleres player.<sup>*</sup></li>
    </ol>

<h2 id="custodia-vigilia"><a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Council_Keleres#Faction_Specific_Components:~:text=Custodia%20Vigilia">Custodia Vigilia</a> <sub>(Legendary Planet)</sub></h2>
    <ol class="note">
    <li>The Custodia Vigilia planet card is gained exhausted.<sup>4</sup></li>
    <li>Units cannot be placed on Custodia Vigilia.<sup>4</sup></li>
    <li>Custodia Vigilia is not on the game board, and does not exist in a system.<sup>2,4</sup></li>
    <li>The Keleres player cannot lose control of Custodia Vigilia.<sup>12</sup></li>
    <ol><li>The Keleres player cannot be eliminated once they control Custodia Vigilia.<sup>4</sup></li></ol>
    <li>Custodia Vigilia may be used to qualify for objectives, if it meets any other requirements listed.<sup>4</sup></li>
    <ol><li>The <a href="/R_production"><sc>Production</sc></a> value that the Custodia Vigilia legendary planet ability gives <a href="/R_mecatol_rex">Mecatol Rex</a> counts toward the <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Objectives#Prophecy_of_Kings_Expansion_4:~:text=Produce%20en%20Masse"><i>Produce en Masse</i></a> objective.<sup>4,9</sup></li></ol>
    <li>Custodia Vigilia counts as a planet for agendas if it meets the specific criteria of those agendas.<sup>4</sup></li>
    <li>Custodia Vigilia only gives command tokens when the Imperial strategy card is used to gain a victory point for controlling <a href="/R_mecatol_rex">Mecatol Rex</a>, not when it is used to score a public objective.<sup>4</sup></li>
    <li>The Keleres player may use a command token to perform the secondary of Imperial during the same strategic action that they gained that token.<sup>*</sup></li>
    <li>When the Keleres player uses the <a href="/R_production"><sc>Production</sc></a> ability of Custodia Vigilia, it is treated as though it were a unit.<sup>4</sup></li>
    <ol><li>This may trigger the abilities of the <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Cybernetic_Technologies#Sarween_Tools"><i>Sarween Tools</i></a> technology, and other similar abilities.<sup>4</sup></li></ol>
    <li>The <a href="/F_ul">Ul</a> player&rsquo;s <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Titans_of_Ul#Faction_Promissory_Note:~:text=Terraform"><i>Terraform</i></a> faction promissory note may be attached to Custodia Vigilia.<sup>4</sup></li>
    <ol><li>If <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Titans_of_Ul#Faction_Promissory_Note:~:text=Terraform"><i>Terraform</i></a> is attached to Custodia Vigilia, it may be explored.<sup>4</sup></li></ol>
    </ol>

<h2 id="artemiris"><a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Council_Keleres#Flagship:~:text=Artemiris">Artemiris</a> <sub>(Flagship)</sub></h2>
    <ol class="note">
    <li>If a player cannot spend two influence, they cannot activate the system containing the <i>Artemiris</i>.<sup>12</sup></li>
    </ol>

<h2 id="xander-alexin-victori-iii"><a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Council_Keleres#Leaders:~:text=Xander%20Alexin%20Victori%20III">Xander Alexin Victori III</a> <sub>(Agent)</sub></h2>
    <ol class="note">
    <li>Xander Alexin Victori III applies to only a single instance of spending trade goods.<sup>4</sup></li>
    </ol>

<h2 id="suffi-an"><a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Council_Keleres#Leaders:~:text=Suffi%20An">Suffi An</a> <sub>(Commander)</sub></h2>
    <ol class="note">
    <li>The trade good to unlock Suffi An is spent after, and independent of, any trade goods spent while resolving the action card.<sup>*</sup></li>
    <li>If the Keleres player uses their additional action to perform another component action, they may perform another additional action. They may do this any number of times.<sup>*</sup></li>
    <li>Suffi An does not trigger from the component action of the action card used that was to unlock her.<sup>*</sup></li>
    <ol><li>If the Keleres player can perform a second action through some other game effect (such as the <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Propulsion_Technologies#Fleet_Logistics"><i>Fleet Logistics</i></a> technology), they may unlock Suffi An by playing an action card with a component action for their first action, then perform a second component action, which will then allow them to perform a third action because of Suffi An.<sup>*</sup></li></ol>
    <li>If a player&rsquo;s turn is ended by a game effect, they cannot use Suffi An to perform an additional action.<sup>*</sup></li>
    <li>A player cannot use Suffi An to pass on the same turn they performed an action.<sup>1</sup></li>
    <li>If a player&rsquo;s additional action would be to use a component action to play an action card, and that card is canceled, they are not required to perform an alternate additional action on that turn.<sup>*</sup></li>
    </ol>

<h2 id="harka-leeds"><a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Council_Keleres#Leaders:~:text=Harka%20Leeds">Harka Leeds</a> &mdash; <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Council_Keleres#Leaders:~:text=Erwan%27s%20Covenant">Erwan&rsquo;s Covenant</a> <sub>(Hero)</sub></h2>
    <ol class="note">
    </ol>

<h2 id="kuuasi-aun-jalatai"><a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Council_Keleres#Leaders:~:text=Kuuasi%20Aun%20Jalatai">Kuuasi Aun Jalatai</a> &mdash; <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Council_Keleres#Leaders:~:text=Overwing%20Zeta">Overwing Zeta</a> <sub>(Hero)</sub></h2>
    <ol class="note">
    <li>The Keleres player must be participating in the combat in order to resolve <i>Overwing Zeta</i>.<sup>4</sup></li>
    <li><i>Overwing Zeta</i> may be played at the start of any round of combat, not just the first.<sup>12</sup></li>
    <ol><li><i>Overwing Zeta</i> may be played in a round following the <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Council_Keleres#Flagship:~:text=Artemiris"><i>Artemiris</i></a> being destroyed.<sup>*</sup></li></ol>
    <li>Ships placed by <i>Overwing Zeta</i> count against the Keleres player&rsquo;s fleet pool immediately; any excess non&ndash;fighter ships are removed at once.<sup>2</sup></li>
    <li>If a player wishes to place a ship, but there are none of that type left in their reinforcements, they may remove a ship of that type from any system that does not contain one of their command tokens and place that instead.<sup>1</sup></li>
    </ol>

<h2 id="odlynn-myrr"><a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Council_Keleres#Leaders:~:text=Odlynn%20Myrr">Odlynn Myrr</a> &mdash; <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Council_Keleres#Leaders:~:text=Operation%20Archon">Operation Archon</a> <sub>(Hero)</sub></h2>
    <ol class="note">
    <li>The additional votes are not cast until the Keleres player casts votes normally.<sup>*</sup></li>
    <li>The Keleres player may vote for a different outcome than the one they predicted. If they do, they will gain one trade good and one command token.<sup>*</sup></li>
    <li>The Keleres player will still receive the trade goods and command tokens if the agenda is discarded and resolved with no effect by the <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Action_Cards#Prophecy_of_Kings:~:text=Deadly%20Plot"><i>Deadly Plot</i></a> action card.<sup>*</sup></li>
    </ol>

<h2 id="omniopiares"><a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Council_Keleres#Mech:~:text=Omniopiares">Omniopiares</a> <sub>(Mech)</sub></h2>
    <ol class="note">
    <li>If a planet contains multiple mechs, the invading player must pay one influence for each, as separate payments.<sup>2,4</sup></li>
    </ol>
</article>
